--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT SHIPPED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI RouteEfficiencyPage at web parity: a pure @Observable state holder
(ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injectable RouteEfficiencyDataSource seam whose method
names mirror the web hooks at the Swift call sites (loadVehicles ← useSelectedVehicle/GET /vehicles;
useRouteEfficiency ← GET /analytics/route-efficiency?vehicle_id&start&end). Every web useMemo
derivation is ported (totalTrips, bestEff=min, worstEff=max, avgEff=mean, chartData=sort-by-avg
.prefix(10)). Consumption (Wh/km) and distance convert to the user's unit ONLY at the render boundary
via the shared Units facade + RouteEfficiencyFormat (ADR-005); the model holds the analytics-endpoint
shape verbatim.

The page reproduces the web chrome (PageContainer title + subtitle + the global VehicleSelect + the
RangePicker date filter) and ALL of the web's sections:

  GlassPanel1  — RouteEfficiencySummarySection: four-up routes / total-trips / best / avg-efficiency.
  GlassPanel2  — RouteEfficiencyRouteCard grid: per-route TSGlassPanel cards (IconBox, start→end,
                 variant-tinted average-consumption Badge, best/avg/worst proportional bar + numbers);
                 common.noData EmptyState when there are no routes.
  Route-Efficiency-Comparison — RouteEfficiencyComparisonSection: TSChartContainer hosting the native
                 Swift Charts grouped TSBarChart of best/avg/worst per route (green/cyan/red, top ten
                 by average), a colored legend, the route-label axis, the exportable CSV; the
                 chartData.length>1 guard shows the chart's empty state otherwise.
  GlassPanel4  — RouteEfficiencyMetricsSection: best / avg / worst efficiency bars + most-driven-route
                 trip bar, or the common.noData EmptyState.

Adaptive (ADR-002/006): header, summary grid, route-card grid, and metrics grid reflow for macOS /
iPad regular vs. compact iPhone. All copy resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names
(18 new bare routeEfficiency.* keys added; common.noData already present). a11y labels on panels +
chart; Dynamic Type; light/dark via design tokens (no hardcoded colors/typography). Loading state =
.redacted skeleton; empty/error/success modeled by RouteEfficiencyPhase.

Navigation (mirrors the sibling unrouted DriveDetailRouteRegistration; .driving host is owned by
DriveScorePage): typed RouteEfficiencyLink + .routeEfficiencyDestination() NavigationDestination +
RouteEfficiencyRouteRegistration.make() factory, with deep-link path "/route-efficiency" → .driving
added to AppRouteParser.aliases (like "/drive-score").

Files (apps/apple/Sources/Features/Driving/):
  RouteEfficiencyPageModel.swift          — @Observable model, types, phase, data-source protocol
  RouteEfficiencyPageModel.Sample.swift   — Sample / Empty / Failing data sources
  RouteEfficiencyFormat.swift             — display-boundary formatters (efficiency/distance/variant)
  RouteEfficiencyPage.swift               — View + header + phase switch + previews
  RouteEfficiencyPage.Panels.swift        — summary / route cards / metrics panels + bars
  RouteEfficiencyPage.Charts.swift        — comparison ChartContainer + BarChart
  RouteEfficiencyPage.Chrome.swift        — RangePicker control + loading skeleton
  RouteEfficiencyRouteRegistration.swift  — typed-link NavigationDestination + factory
Tests (apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Driving/):
  RouteEfficiencyPageModelTests.swift     — 9 state-machine/derivation tests
  RouteEfficiencyFormatTests.swift        — 9 formatter tests
Edited: apps/apple/Sources/App/AppRouteParser.swift (alias), apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings (18 keys)

