PRE-EXISTING BASE UNBLOCKS (out-of-nominal-scope; required to make the SHARED build+test gate
RUNNABLE under Xcode 26.5 / Swift 6.3.2 — each is minimal + behavior-preserving + lint-clean + fully
disclosed here per honesty covenant #9 "no silent drift"). None are RouteEfficiency files; all fail
identically on the untouched base; my changes only make the tree compile.)
  1. Sources/Features/Diagnostics/AnomalyDashboardModels.swift:185 — the chained dictionary
     `.map { … }.sorted { … }` hit "compiler is unable to type-check this expression in reasonable
     time" (blocks the WHOLE app build). Split into an annotated intermediate + sorted step exactly
     as the compiler prescribes; identical result.
  2. Tests/Unit/Features/Admin/VehicleCostPageModelTests.swift — @MainActor static `zeroTotals`
     referenced by the nonisolated StubSource → marked `nonisolated` (VehicleCostTotals is Sendable);
     and XCTAssertEqual(accuracy:) on Date values → compare .timeIntervalSince1970 (Date is not
     FloatingPoint). Same assertions.
  3. Tests/Unit/Features/Driving/DriveDetailFormatTests.swift — non-@MainActor test method calling the
     @MainActor DriveDetailRouteRegistration.make → method marked @MainActor (matches the codebase's
     existing method-level convention, e.g. ChargingHeatmapDerivationsTests).
  4. Tests/Unit/Features/Admin/GDPRExportPageModelTests.swift — nonisolated StubSource calling the
     @MainActor static fixture `artifact(...)` → marked `nonisolated`.
  5. Tests/Unit/Features/Analytics/TimelinePageModelTests.swift — non-@MainActor TimelineFormatTests
     calling the @MainActor TimelinePageModel.utcDayKey → class marked @MainActor.

