PRE-EXISTING BASE ISSUES LEFT UNTOUCHED (unrelated to this page; out of allowed scope; NOT masked —
disclosed honestly rather than "red-as-green")
  - Tests/.../Toast.Tests.swift:183 ToastCenterMutationBridgeTests.testMutationFailedUsesLocalizedErrorDetail
    fails at RUNTIME: expects title "Failed to save" (the caller's fallback) but mutationFailed yields
    "Something went wrong". This is a genuine, AMBIGUOUS Toast localization behavior (the caller's
    fallback appears to be shadowed) — possibly a real product bug, NOT a stale-test/compile issue.
    Fixing it would require Toast domain intent I do not own and risks masking a real defect, so it is
    left as-is. It is the ONLY failure among 25,472 unit tests and is unrelated to RouteEfficiency.
  - TeslaSync/feature-views/AnomalyInlineRow.Previews.swift:37,89 (+2) — pre-existing line_length
    violations under project-wide `swiftlint --strict`. Outside the gate's Features/Driving lint scope
    and unrelated to this page.

